stateDiagram-v2
  accTitle: Proposed B6 activity lifecycle state machine
  accDescr: A proposed lifecycle distinguishes ready, reserved, running, preemption requested, interruption requested, suspended, resume check, unsuccessful stopped, and verified completed states. Resumption is guarded by renewed evidence, permission, budget, and external-state checks.
  [*] --> READY
  READY --> RESERVED: capacity reserved
  RESERVED --> RUNNING: dispatch confirmed
  RESERVED --> READY: reservation released
  RUNNING --> PREEMPT_REQUESTED: higher priority work
  RUNNING --> INTERRUPT_REQUESTED: risk or policy event
  RUNNING --> COMPLETED: verified postconditions
  RUNNING --> STOPPED: terminal refusal or budget exhaustion
  PREEMPT_REQUESTED --> SUSPENDED: safe checkpoint
  INTERRUPT_REQUESTED --> SUSPENDED: safe boundary reached
  INTERRUPT_REQUESTED --> STOPPED: cannot safely continue
  SUSPENDED --> RESUME_CHECK: resume requested
  RESUME_CHECK --> RUNNING: all guards pass
  RESUME_CHECK --> SUSPENDED: resource or approval pending
  RESUME_CHECK --> STOPPED: stale or invalid state
  COMPLETED --> [*]
  STOPPED --> [*]
